    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d9">

                <pb facs="0048" n="16" xml:id="pg16"/>

                <head>9. Telegram From the Embassy in Cuba to the Department of State<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d9-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Havana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1958-01-31T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 31,
                                1958—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>424. Reference Deptel 394 [384?].<anchor n="2" xml:id="d9-f2"/>Deptel 384 not
                    received here until January 30. I will inform Batista through Guell as
                    instructed second paragraph 384.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d9-f3"/> Re procedure
                    suggested final paragraph 384 I recommend approval these three requests and
                    delivery when ready unless situation significantly changed in meantime. As
                    general policy I believe US should honor reasonable requests recommended by
                    Military mission as long as GOC proceeds along lines acceptable to US. Holding
                    back on each request to force GOC step by step seems petty and as likely to
                    thwart our objective as to attain it.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d9-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d9-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 737.56/1–3158. Secret; Priority.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d9-f2" n="2" xml:id="d9-f2-content">
                <p><ref target="#d7">Document 7</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d9-f3" n="3" xml:id="d9-f3-content">
                <p>In telegram 431 from Havana, February 4, Smith reported that he had informed
                    Batista through Guell as instructed in the second paragraph of telegram 384.
                    (Department of State, Central Files, 737.56/2–458)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
